#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078170 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "697f9bd8-9edf-5643-8cdb-a821b6dce09c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle by Completing the Square"}] :question/id #uuid "36c32777-8081-5431-a112-321738a3adab" :question/math-academy-id "e-3228" :question/problem "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is $x^2 + y^2 - 4x + 6y = 12$." :question/worked-solution "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} + y^{2} - 4x + 6y &= 12 \\\\\n(x^{2} - 4x) + (y^{2} + 6y) &= 12 \\\\\n(x^{2} - 2 \\cdot 2x + 2^{2}) + (y^{2} + 2 \\cdot 3y + 3^{2}) &= 12 + 2^{2} + 3^{2} \\\\\n(x^{2} - 2 \\cdot 2x + 2^{2}) + (y^{2} + 2 \\cdot 3y + 3^{2}) &= 25\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 2)^{2} + (y + 3)^{2} &= 5^{2} \\\\\n(x - 2)^{2} + (y - (-3))^{2} &= 5^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(2,-3)$ and its radius is $5$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078171 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98e3f3b4-8dfa-515c-90b1-09fb19d68144" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle by Completing the Square with Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "b05d1090-fd7b-52eb-84a7-55377ead0dda" :question/math-academy-id "e-3229" :question/problem "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is $x^2 + y^2 - x = 6$." :question/worked-solution "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} + y^{2} - x &= 6 \\\\\n(x^{2} - x) + y^{2} &= 6 \\\\\n(x^{2} - 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x + (\\frac{1}{2})^{2}) + y^{2} &= 6 + (\\frac{1}{2})^{2} \\\\\n(x^{2} - 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x + (\\frac{1}{2})^{2}) + y^{2} &= \\frac{25}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect square and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - \\frac{1}{2})^{2} + y^{2} &= (\\frac{5}{2})^{2} \\\\\n(x - \\frac{1}{2})^{2} + (y - 0)^{2} &= (\\frac{5}{2})^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}, 0 \\right)\n$$\n\nand its radius is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5}{2}\n$$"}]}
